The largest response is after conjunctions and relative-clause openers, rather
than ordinary list items. Discourse words and auxiliaries get smaller responses.
A short text tail distinguishes a whole word from a token suffix (e.g. 'or'
in a name), and demonstrative 'that' from clause-opening 'that'.
Other tokens are background (zero), except a small negative document-start mean.
